> API and interpretation

The machine is epsilon-free: this API does not perform epsilon closure. Partial
mode records missing moves as-1 and omits an empty initial subset; complete mode
retains a rejecting empty trap. Numbering is native discovery order, not
arbitrary subset-bit order. The optional output-state cap bounds created
subsets, not every union temporary or peak RAM. The2^n curve is a mathematical
reference for this family, not an observed count copied into results.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

